---
/**
 * Pricing: what's free, what HD credits buy, and what an HD run costs. Paddle's
 * review needs prices and what a purchase includes, reachable from the site.
 * Packs and run costs come from server/pricing.ts, which the server charges by.
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
import { REFUND_DAYS } from '../data/legal'
import { COST, PACKS, UPSCALE, usd } from '../../../../server/pricing'
---

<Page title="Pricing · Inlay" description="Inlay is free. Optional HD mode is paid for with credit packs that never expire.">
  <article class="prose" aria-labelledby="pricing-title">
    <h1 id="pricing-title">Pricing</h1>
    <p class="lede">Inlay is free. HD mode, for the hardest images, is optional and paid for with credits.</p>

    <h2>Free, with no account</h2>
    <p>Everything the <a href="/app/">app</a> does in your browser is free, has no limits and needs no account. That won't change.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Tracing with every preset: logo, illustration, line art, pixel art, poster and centerline.</li>
      <li>The editor: recolour, merge, move, reshape and mirror shapes.</li>
      <li>Background removal and upscaling in your browser.</li>
      <li>Batch tracing, and export to SVG, PNG, PDF, EPS and DXF.</li>
      <li>The <a href="/docs/package/getting-started/">npm package</a>, MIT licensed.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>HD mode</h2>
    <p>
      HD mode runs on our servers, for images that are too large or too difficult to do well in a browser. Your image is uploaded, processed
      and deleted as soon as the result is back. You choose it image by image, and it shows a free low-resolution preview first.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Tracing a big image at its full size, for finer detail than the browser's 2048 px trace.</li>
      <li>Upscaling a small image 4× with a larger model than the browser's, before you trace it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>HD mode is in beta. Both are in the app's export panel, offered when they'd help the image you've opened.</p>

    <h2>Credit packs</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Pack</th><th class="num">Price</th><th class="num">Per credit</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          PACKS.map((p) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{p.credits} credits</td>
              <td class="num">{usd(p.usd)}</td>
              <td class="num">{usd(p.usd / p.credits)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Prices are in US dollars. Sales tax or VAT is added where it applies; you'll see the total before you pay. Credits never expire. Buying
      credits needs an account (an email address; no password).
    </p>

    <h2>What an HD trace costs</h2>
    <p>
      One credit isn't one image: the cost depends on the image's size, and the app shows it before anything is uploaded. While HD is in
      beta these costs may change; we'll update this page first.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Image size</th><th class="num">Credits</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          COST.map((c) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{c.label}</td>
              <td class="num">{c.credits}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>HD upscaling costs {UPSCALE.credits} credits an image, for images up to {UPSCALE.maxPixels / 1_000_000} megapixels (about 700 × 700).</p>
    <p>If an HD run fails, its credits go straight back to your account.</p>

    <h2>Payments and refunds</h2>
    <p>
      Payments are handled by Paddle, our reseller and the Merchant of Record for all orders: it takes the payment, charges any tax and emails
      your receipt. You can ask for a full refund within {REFUND_DAYS} days of buying; see the <a href="/refunds/">refund policy</a>. Buying
      credits means agreeing to the <a href="/terms/">terms</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Page>
